or, Part Five - Penny Arcade </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2006/05/29/the-song-of-the-sorcelator-part-five\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2006/05/29/the-song-of-the-sorcelator-part-five </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Videogaming-related online strip by Mike Krahulik and Jerry Holkins. Includes news and commentary. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* No, but it makes a good story.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-10-2020, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T14:30:38-07:00","id":1395912,"title":"","content":"There's no &quot;requirement&quot; on having had bad things happen, and when I'm running a game I generally don't mandate players put certain things into their backstory (unless it's a particular theme for a campaign like, &quot;Why are you all here together?&quot;) but that said I do ask players to include plot hooks for me and having bad things happen in a past allows for more hooks than having had a wonderful perfect past. At the least, throw in some rivals or other people who are unhappy with how perfect the character's life was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T22:52:13-07:00","id":1395973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1395454#post1395454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Storyteller is new? Right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Our first game ended cos the ST felt it was going nowhere and we are restarting in this 2nd game in the dark ages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T04:35:57-07:00","id":1395990,"title":"","content":"When you play vampire, it pays to be instigators. You should all have wants<br /> <br /> -I want control over this company<br /> -I want this place to be recognized as my domain<br /> -I want to host elysiums<br /> -I want a huge herd<br /> -I want this person on my side<br /> -I want to learn blood magic (and not get caught in a Tremere trap)<br /> -I want to avenge an injustice I felt as a mortal (The so called &quot;list of kids who bullied you in highschool&quot; is rather fun) <br /> -I want to fulfill my sire's wish of removing his rival. <br /> -I want to build up defences because my sire's rivals may come after me. <br /> <br /> You should try to work everything your ST throws at you into fulfilling your ambitions, and you should try to achieve them yourself when he isn't throwing anything pressing at you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T05:08:13-07:00","id":1395993,"title":"","content":"I want that cute Anarch to like me...<br /> <br /> (Mostly kidding but not 100% \ud83d\ude0a)<br /> <br /> Seriously. Most of my characters have some negative elements in their backstory but your character can be totally normal and well-adjusted till your Embrace. After that your life is probably gonna suck. At least for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T06:04:47-07:00","id":1396005,"title":"","content":"I like tragedy and the fact that there's somethings called Greek Mythology and Greek Tragedy means to me that tragedy don't have to be angsty or whatever.<br /> <br /> And I do think that tragedy fits Vampire as a theme better than empowerment does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T06:40:06-07:00","id":1396012,"title":"","content":"There's a happy mid point between the power fantasy of early editions and the &quot;you should kill yourself&quot; of the last edition.<br /> <br /> But I suppose the power fantasy is there to compensate for the suck.<br /> <br /> Even a well adjusted kindred must bare with the fact that he or she probably only has an average of 8 hours of being awake each day, potentially with wonderful winters and miserable summers. There's no getting around that. But being able to have fawning devotees or being able to kick a man's knee inwards in a spectacular manner is good stress relief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T07:51:31-07:00","id":1396019,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"970\" data-vbnamecard=\"970\">Gurkhal</a> I like both tragedy and angst but tragedy is definitely deeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T11:15:15-07:00","id":1396044,"title":"","content":"From my opinion there is no need for a tragic backstory in the 4 big lines because if you suddenly awaken as hungry dead or a choleric monster as a normal unknown human it is tragic enough alone.For Mage there is no need for tragic because it is a hopeful game and about Changeling I can not say anything. But in HTR, Wr and DTF there should be one because without one there is hardly a believ why you even should be one without one and in Demon you are a Fallen Angel so it can not be not tragedy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T12:01:24-07:00","id":1396050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1395993#post1395993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want that cute Anarch to like me...<br /> <br /> (Mostly kidding but not 100% \ud83d\ude0a)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think &quot;notice me, sempai&quot; is the motivation for at least two or three characters in the original Chicago by Night.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T12:28:13-07:00","id":1396058,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> thanks. That actually validates my feelings on this issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T04:54:44-07:00","id":1396157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1395990#post1395990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you play vampire, it pays to be instigators. You should all have wants<br /> <br /> -I want control over this company<br /> -I want this place to be recognized as my domain<br /> -I want to host elysiums<br /> -I want a huge herd<br /> -I want this person on my side<br /> -I want to learn blood magic (and not get caught in a Tremere trap)<br /> -I want to avenge an injustice I felt as a mortal (The so called &quot;list of kids who bullied you in highschool&quot; is rather fun)<br /> -I want to fulfill my sire's wish of removing his rival.<br /> -I want to build up defences because my sire's rivals may come after me.<br /> <br /> You should try to work everything your ST throws at you into fulfilling your ambitions, and you should try to achieve them yourself when he isn't throwing anything pressing at you.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> I disagree with the idea that happy people don't become adventurers. A person's capacity for desire - greed, ambition, altruism, glory-seeking, etc. - is unquenchable, even if they otherwise have nothing particularly bad going for them. They want MORE, and one way or another have determined that adventuring is the way to satisfy this ache.<br /> <br /> Obviously, both the circumstances that led to the Embrace and the new vampiric state establish a baseline of tragedy that all Kindred must reckon with, the life leading up to it and the unlife following the &quot;transition period&quot; might be light on suffering, as it were. The character gets involved with the plot - or, as MyWifeIsScary alluded to, MAKES the plot - because they think they have something to gain. Even if that something is intangible (glory, &quot;the greater good&quot;, fun), or illusory (&quot;taking my rightful place as monarch of the Martian principalities&quot;, said the Malkavian, without a hint of irony or embarrassment).<br /> <br /> If this were D&amp;D, let's say, it would be much the same. The Fighter wants to establish a kingdom by his own hand. The Cleric wants to rid the countryside of infernal influence and establish a temple to their god's majesty. The Wizard wants to built a wizard's tower and stock it with ancient tomes of forgotten lore, rescuing the knowledge from obscurity. The Rogue really, really likes works of art for purely aesthetic (or prestige) reasons, and is willing to steal them.<br /> <br /> All that changes with Kindred PCs is the exact nature of they &quot;projects&quot;. The Ventrue sees Kindred society as another ladder to climb. The Tremere has all the time in the world to study magic - an intellectual good unto itself - and that eternity isn't nearly enough to learn all they want to (which is everything). The Gangrel controls a number of cattle farms to feed them, but thinks they could always use a bigger business (and a bigger share of the local beef market). The Malkavian, obsessive compulsive, thinks economic and social inequality is bullshit (because it applies &quot;the rules&quot; unevenly between groups and social classes, and that's unacceptable), and is going to take everything over so they can MAKE it all make sense, despite the system not really being a detriment to them personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T05:34:34-07:00","id":1396162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396157#post1396157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with the idea that happy people don't become adventurers. A person's capacity for desire - greed, ambition, altruism, glory-seeking, etc. - is unquenchable, even if they otherwise have nothing particularly bad going for them. They want MORE, and one way or another have determined that adventuring is the way to satisfy this ache.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a person was happy and content in their life, they by definition wouldn't be desiring more or different things. Humans have a nasty habit of subconsciously wanting all kinds of things while never realizing it consciously. This is part of the reason why they stay in jobs they hate, maintain relationships that are toxic, or keep bad habits. Vampirism tends to remove some of the primary motivators to adventure. The fear of getting old and missing out on life is no longer applicable, as long as you have access to blood and sunlight shelter there is no end date to existence. <br /> <br /> VtM might weave tragedy into every characters story, it also caters to a psychology pattern that is quite the opposite of the classical &quot;adventurer&quot; mindset. Vampires are supposed to stay in their cities due to real or imagined danger of lupines. So from the beginning they don't go far afield as a base line. Then the fact that they can't move about during daylight makes the characters less likely to travel due to time constraints and means they rarely stray far from their haven, let alone their city. Sure there is the random mobile Brujah biker gang or group of Gangrel wandering about, but the majority of vampires tend to stay put.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T07:09:22-07:00","id":1396163,"title":"","content":"If I am not useful, I will be disposed of<br /> If I am too useful, I will be disposed of<br /> If I gain power too slowly, I will be disposed of<br /> If I gain power to quickly, I will be disposed of. <br /> <br /> Just because you're immortal doesn't mean you've got all the time in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T15:26:57-07:00","id":1396223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396163#post1396163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I am not useful, I will be disposed of<br /> If I am too useful, I will be disposed of<br /> If I gain power too slowly, I will be disposed of<br /> If I gain power to quickly, I will be disposed of.<br /> <br /> Just because you're immortal doesn't mean you've got all the time in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.<br /> <br /> If you are playing in a game with grossly over inflated vampire population numbers, then yes you have near constant game of thrones power plays and body counts. Alternatively if you are playing with the suggested ratios, then a city the size of San Francisco would have like six kindred total at any given time. Such a small population basically means there is no Camarilla, Sabbat, or any other organized power structure. It would just be a single coterie running the town or a few vampires who have their own niches in society and just quietly co-exist.<br /> <br /> VtM has always has this strange fluff dichotomy that gives the impression that every vampire is a cursed loner, doomed to suffer through an eternal night in crushing isolation, while some how simultaneously being just one vampire amongst hundreds that are churned out by the elders for their insane plots. I get that VtM capitalizes on teenage angst and turbulent emotions, but after a certain point you have to pick a world state.<br /> <br /> The real reason is of course creating fertile grounds for storytelling, which means the end of the world is always nigh, the power structure is always unstable, the given elder is always teetering on the edge of insanity, the enemies are always laying siege to the gates, there is always the threat of being replaced or being seen as a threat, etc. This goes back to the original post about there must be tragedy in a characters backstory, either the characters history or their situation has to act as a story catalyst to promote the game play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T15:48:16-07:00","id":1396227,"title":"","content":"WoD cities have higher populations, so you'd get more kindred in a 'ideal ratio' San francisco. besides that, games dont really take place in ideal ratio cities. plus in small cities there are generally smaller racks. I agree with you that there are places with too few people to set up a bloated government. <br /> <br /> but you would only really play a small city game when there is some sort of external threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:44:05-07:00","id":1396244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396223#post1396223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and no.<br /> <br /> If you are playing in a game with grossly over inflated vampire population numbers, then yes you have near constant game of thrones power plays and body counts. Alternatively if you are playing with the suggested ratios, then a city the size of San Francisco would have like six kindred total at any given time. Such a small population basically means there is no Camarilla, Sabbat, or any other organized power structure. It would just be a single coterie running the town or a few vampires who have their own niches in society and just quietly co-exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've mentioned this elsewhere but 1:100,000 was the suggested ratio for a SAFE AND HIDDEN Kindred population.<br /> <br /> The game also stated that vampires were grossly overpopulated and gathered in major cities rather than spread out.<br /> <br /> There are no vampires in Bumfuck, Nowhere but there's 200 vampires in, say, New York.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T18:25:58-07:00","id":1396266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396244#post1396244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are no vampires in Bumfuck, Nowhere but there's 200 vampires in, say, New York.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the irony being that in NYC, they probably don't stand out as much.<br /> <br /> (In my own head cannon, NYC was largely Camarilla, largely just because I wanted a Prince and then a set of &quot;Dukes&quot; over each borough, with one of those Dukes being a Brujah who looked like Isaac Hayes. Don't judge me.)<br /> <br /> And I think that next year for April Fools Day, we should have Bumfuck by Night on the STV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:23:08-07:00","id":1396468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396244#post1396244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've mentioned this elsewhere but 1:100,000 was the suggested ratio for a SAFE AND HIDDEN Kindred population.<br /> <br /> The game also stated that vampires were grossly overpopulated and gathered in major cities rather than spread out.<br /> <br /> There are no vampires in Bumfuck, Nowhere but there's 200 vampires in, say, New York.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just &quot;safe and hidden&quot; it is the entire world population of vampires, which includes those that are awake, in torpor, newly made, elder vampires, and oh yeah.... the entire Kuei-Jin population of the world.<br /> <br /> Here is a quote from the Vampire Storytellers Handbook, 3rd Edition WW2304 published back in 2000.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201c<b>How many vampires are there, anyway?</b><br /> <br /> From a strictly Cainite point of view, probably around 40,000. The Middle Kingdom has roughly 20,000 Kuei-jin, for a grand total of approximately 60,000 \u2013 one for every 100,000 people on the planet. <br /> Of those Kindred, the clans make up the enormous majority of the population, leaving the rare bloodlines, fallen clans and other, less-quantifiable vampires at about 2,000 vampires in total. Cities aren't likely to have more than one or two Harbingers of Skulls or Gargoyles, if they have any at all. In fact, most cities don't have any Kindred other than those of the clans \u2013 and that's precisely how the clans like it. It is, after all, better to deal with the devil you know.\u2026\u201d </div> </div> </div>So there is a stated max population for vampires, and it is lower than most people think due to the Kuei-jin numbers messing with the math. But more importantly once you start allocating the population by clan and bloodline, and then finally adjust for how many vampires are inactive (torpor, trapped in other dimensions, etc.) The number of active vampires in any given city starts plummeting real fast.<br /> <br /> I mean depending on how you look at it the torpor/inactive percentage goes from 20% to 50% of the vampire population. This in turn makes having 200 cainite vampires in a city about 1/200th of the global cainite population, with a 50% inactive ratio that becomes a 1/100th portion.<br /> <br /> In short when you boost up the numbers in one section of the world, large swaths of the rest of the world technically wouldn't have any vampire population.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:27:01-07:00","id":1396469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396468#post1396468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not just &quot;safe and hidden&quot; it is the entire world population of vampires, which includes those that are awake, in torpor, newly made, elder vampires, and oh yeah.... the entire Kuei-Jin population of the world.<br /> <br /> Here is a quote from the Vampire Storytellers Handbook, 3rd Edition WW2304 published back in 2000.</div> </div> </div> </div>That number is different from the original 1:100,000.<br /> <br /> It's also since been retconned by Word of God.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.redd.it/9dlejy9e09w41.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.redd.it/9dlejy9e09w41.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.redd.it/9dlejy9e09w41.png\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.redd.it/9dlejy9e09w41.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:43:22-07:00","id":1396478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396469#post1396469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That number is different from the original 1:100,000.<br /> <br /> It's also since been retconned by Word of God.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://i.redd.it/9dlejy9e09w41.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.redd.it/9dlejy9e09w41.png</a></div> </div> </div> </div>So your statement is that some one invoked &quot;what ever works in your game&quot; rule (which has been in every book since first edition) and that some how counts as a retcon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:47:19-07:00","id":1396482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396478#post1396478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So your statement is that some one invoked &amp;quot;what ever works in your game&amp;quot; rule (which has been in every book since first edition) and that some how counts as a retcon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think 1:100k work just fine. No need to invoke matias Hopkins commentary on reddit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:52:35-07:00","id":1396483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396478#post1396478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So your statement is that some one invoked &quot;what ever works in your game&quot; rule (which has been in every book since first edition) and that some how counts as a retcon?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, from the original books before then, which I assumed people knew about.<br /> <br /> Also, Matthew Dawkins later statement for now.<br /> <br /> And Twitter page not reddit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:03:22-07:00","id":1396537,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Thoth;n1396223]<br /> <br /> Yes and no.<br /> <br /> VtM has always has this strange fluff dichotomy that gives the impression that every vampire is a cursed loner, doomed to suffer through an eternal night in crushing isolation, while some how simultaneously being just one vampire amongst hundreds that are churned out by the elders for their insane plots. I get that VtM capitalizes on teenage angst and turbulent emotions, but after a certain point you have to pick a world state.<br /> <br /> I like to think of Kindred society as a small exclusive high school or college/university. Not total crushing isolation, but not hundreds of neonates existing solely as cannon fodder either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:37:53-07:00","id":1396556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396537#post1396537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to think of Kindred society as a small exclusive high school or college/university. Not total crushing isolation, but not hundreds of neonates existing solely as cannon fodder either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I use high school as an easy analogy. The Kindred are MONSTROUSLY petty, cliquish, and divided but all of them are aware of the names of the others in their city unless you're at one of the largest cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T02:38:14-07:00","id":1396631,"title":"","content":"Cities are really large, but you're all fighting over the main spots; The nightlife districts aren't usually that big and nobody cares about suburbia. if you're in a really big city the chances are you'll be fighting over local important things in your part of the city with vampires in your part of the city. The other parts of the big city might as well be a different city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T02:48:45-07:00","id":1396635,"title":"","content":"A character who had a pretty good life actually could be a very good candidate for roleplaying angst as a vampire. Imagine, for example, Johnny Cage from the original Mortal Kombat movie.<br /> <br /> &quot;Liu, I hate this place. I do. I'm telling ya, I hate it. I'm in a hostile environment, I am completely unprepared. I'm surrounded by people who probably wanna kick my ass... it's like being back in high school!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's how every Neonate from a place of privilege should act if they're NOT Embraced into the Ventrue, Toreador, or Tremere low gen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T06:50:38-07:00","id":1396668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396635#post1396635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's how every Neonate from a place of privilege should act if they're NOT Embraced into the Ventrue, Toreador, or Tremere low gen.</div> </div> </div> </div>And hell, even Neonates from those three Clans should feel like everyone wants to kick their ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T07:35:44-07:00","id":1396675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396635#post1396635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character who had a pretty good life actually could be a very good candidate for roleplaying angst as a vampire. Imagine, for example, Johnny Cage from the original Mortal Kombat movie.<br /> <br /> &quot;Liu, I hate this place. I do. I'm telling ya, I hate it. I'm in a hostile environment, I am completely unprepared. I'm surrounded by people who probably wanna kick my ass... it's like being back in high school!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's how every Neonate from a place of privilege should act if they're NOT Embraced into the Ventrue, Toreador, or Tremere low gen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Privilege has nothing to do with it, unlike humans who have to wait and see if their offspring grow up into worthwhile individuals, vampires select who gets embraced from an adult population pool. Sure there are random embraces by some but the majority are considered carefully by their sires.<br /> <br /> But what does a sire look for in a potential childer? Some might choose based off looks or a resemblance to a lost love, but by in large childer are selected for their ability to survive and be competent in their abilities. I mean if the local sheriff is looking for some additional muscle to add to his brute squad he could check out a local house wives late night book club meeting or the sheriff could access the local VA records and see which combat veterans are in the area. By the same thought process Ventrue tend to embrace those who are competent business people in life.<br /> <br /> In short you have to ask your self if vampires can choose to embrace some one from special forces groups, fortune 500 companies, the best scientists and artists of a generation..... what would be the benefit of embracing bob the plumber or betty the flouriest? Then ask the question of if vampires are so carefully managing their recruiting, doesn't that mean over time the majority of vampire society is consisting of these types of individuals?<br /> <br /> In a strange way vampire society has many aspects of a meritocracy when it comes to the embrace. If anything excessive privilege could be seen as making one too soft to survive in the vampire world.<br /> <br /> But we know why the fluff alternatives between saying vampires embrace only the best and they embrace on a whim. Its to give character and story options, rather than a functional simulation of how a vampire society would function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T07:37:36-07:00","id":1396677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396675#post1396675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Privilege has nothing to do with it, unlike humans who have to wait and see if their offspring grow up into worthwhile individuals, vampires select who gets embraced from an adult population pool. Sure there are random embraces by some but the majority are considered carefully by their sires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is remotely the case for a large number of Embraces. Plenty of people get Embraced on the spur of the moment based on frenzying, overfeeding, Toreador flaw, a subject dying, or whim.<br /> <br /> There's also people who will be Embraced on immediate need.<br /> <br /> &quot;I need a vampire lawyer or a rich guy to bail me out or a soldier for the cause.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In short you have to ask your self if vampires can choose to embrace some one from special forces groups, fortune 500 companies, the best scientists and artists of a generation..... what would be the benefit of embracing bob the plumber or betty the flouriest? Then ask the question of if vampires are so carefully managing their recruiting, doesn't that mean over time the majority of vampire society is consisting of these types of individuals? </div> </div> </div>I imagine the vast majority of Kindred Embraces are going to be people who can properly disappeared. You can't Embrace Rhianna or Elon Musk. That would be too dangerous to the Masquerade. You can maybe Embrace Rhianna's backup singer or someone who might have become Rhianna should circumstances have not been them. Maybe Elon Musk's right hand man.<br /> <br /> Bob the Plumber or Betty the Florist have as high a chance of being Embraced as, say, Paul the Navy Seal too because it's as likely they'd be Embraced by someone who loves them like their boyfriend or girlfriend who feed on them regularly as Paul for his skillz.<br /> <br /> But that's just my take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But we know why the fluff alternatives between saying vampires embrace only the best and they embrace on a whim. Its to give character and story options, rather than a functional simulation of how a vampire society would function. </div> </div> </div>I think history has shown that the vast majority of human decisions are governed by emotion rather than cold logic and that would certainly apply to the relatively easy act of granting immortality via a bit of blood after feeding.<br /> <br /> YMMV of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-15-2020, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T07:53:09-07:00","id":1396679,"title":"","content":"And those embraces are purged pretty fast. Spur of the moment embraces will result in two executions more often than not, most 'spur' embraces will be fixed within a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T08:39:47-07:00","id":1396683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396679#post1396679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And those embraces are purged pretty fast. Spur of the moment embraces will result in two executions more often than not, most 'spur' embraces will be fixed within a week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which is a major reason why the Camarilla has failed and the Anarch movement exists. We see it canonized in Bloodlines. The scummy piece of shit La Croix tries to destroy a &quot;Bad Embrace&quot; and their sire only to have the entire city turn against him.<br /> <br /> Good riddance to tyrants. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T10:43:56-07:00","id":1396692,"title":"","content":"LaCroix is neither a good example of a prince, nor a ventrue. People hated him because he was an overcompensating toff dickhead with neither brains nor charisma, and you are saved in court by pent up resentment. your average prince could've ordered your mortal family dead to the 18th generation and recieved, at worst, grudging looks. <br /> <br /> You can and should levy heavy punishments on people who embrace. Letting just anyone embrace is selfish indulgence. I mean, If Steve just embraces Ted and is forgiven, when Alice has worked hard to get embrace permission, Alice is going to be pissed off. Moreso, If Jeff was planning on embracing Sarah, and Steve has just embraced Ted, doesn't that make it harder to justify embracing Sarah when there is only so much food for an increased number of mouths? Alice and Jeff should be furious with Steve, and the prince can right that wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T11:19:04-07:00","id":1396698,"title":"","content":"Yeah, unauthorized embraces must be harshly punished, at minimum with death for the childe and probably the sire as well. That is probably the most important law of the Camarilla. You can\u2019t have a vampiric organization if anybody can embrace on a whim, in fact you can\u2019t have the Masquerade if that is allowed. Free embracing would spiral out of control until the Masquerade collapsed, maybe until human and vampire society collapsed too. The Camarilla is wise to prohibit unauthorized embraces and punish offenders harshly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T11:57:53-07:00","id":1396707,"title":"","content":"Creating new vampires is always a bad idea because it's a dread curse and never works out the way you want it to. However, that doesn't mean that it's not something that vampires want to do and do often. It's also listed as one of the major factors for the Anarch Movement in ANARCHS UNBOUND and why many ancilla revolt against the Prince. Prince's attempt to make sure only their supporters Embrace and their less valued citizens don't. Usually, it's for good reason as a Neonate Embracing their dying grandmother isn't going to help anyone.<br /> <br /> However, the Camarilla's fear of Neonates and overpopulation went too far and they re-introduced the position of Scourge to reduce the surplus population. The torture, murder, and execution of anyone who wasn't presented to the Prince plus Thin Bloods just made them look like monsters. Well, more than just being vampires","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T14:20:29-07:00","id":1396728,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> once again I agree with your analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T17:41:31-07:00","id":1396762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396707#post1396707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating new vampires is always a bad idea because it's a dread curse and never works out the way you want it to. However, that doesn't mean that it's not something that vampires want to do and do often. It's also listed as one of the major factors for the Anarch Movement in ANARCHS UNBOUND and why many ancilla revolt against the Prince. Prince's attempt to make sure only their supporters Embrace and their less valued citizens don't. Usually, it's for good reason as a Neonate Embracing their dying grandmother isn't going to help anyone.<br /> <br /> However, the Camarilla's fear of Neonates and overpopulation went too far and they re-introduced the position of Scourge to reduce the surplus population. The torture, murder, and execution of anyone who wasn't presented to the Prince plus Thin Bloods just made them look like monsters. Well, more than just being vampires</div> </div> </div> </div>Well sure, there are plenty of reasons to want to embrace people, which is all the more reason to crack down on the practice with draconian measures. Of course, a Prince will use this law to stack the deck, so to speak, or as a favor to sell. That is a good thing in many regards. It\u2019s good for the Camarilla that only older more influential low generation vampires get to embrace. They are more responsible, wiser and able to pick better candidates, have more resources to introduce the childe into the vampiric world, and they will have a lower generation. Way better do it that way than have a bunch of neonates reproducing like fruit flies, embracing their friends, embracing people who they accidentally kill, making undead gangs, flooding the world with thin blooded caitiff. <br /> <br /> The Tradition of Progeny might be one of the Anarch\u2019s major complaints, but it\u2019s a necessary law and their complaint is a foolish one. Sometimes rebels have a good reason to rebel and sometimes they have a bad reason, and wanting more freedom to embrace is a very bad reason indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T17:55:33-07:00","id":1396766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396762#post1396762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tradition of Progeny might be one of the Anarch\u2019s major complaints, <b>but it\u2019s a necessary law and their complaint is a foolish one. </b>Sometimes rebels have a good reason to rebel and sometimes they have a bad reason, and wanting more freedom to embrace is a very bad reason indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, no it's not. It's just a law that favors one group over another.<br /> <br /> Obviously the other group has no reason to support said law because it works for their enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T18:14:11-07:00","id":1396768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396766#post1396766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, no it's not. It's just a law that favors one group over another.<br /> <br /> Obviously the other group has no reason to support said law because it works for their enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a practice that is necessary for any vampire group to survive. If the Anarchs seize a city, they will have to restrict embraces in that city. The Sabbat can get away with mass embraces during a siege in enemy territory, but they have to restrict embraces too in their territory. If Anarchs are rebelling over a practice that they must themselves adopt if they win, then that makes them either fools or hypocrites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T18:24:01-07:00","id":1396771,"title":"","content":"I would think that the Anarchs would reign in creation to at least some extent, whether this means that the local Baron claims right of creation or the gangs keep their rivals in check. If they didn't it'd only be a matter of time until Bob the Brujah decides to create an undead army of night slaves blood bonded to him and take over. Next, somebody else does the same thing to counter Bob the Brujah. Before you know it, the vampire population is out of control, open warfare starts up, feeding gets sloppy, hunters and the FBI start showing up as the body count grows and it's a bad scene for everyone.<br /> <br /> When it's completely locked down to only those who kiss the Prince's ring get a chance to embrace, it's definitely oppressive. But the law has a certain amount of soundness to it. There's also the argument that the creator needs to be educated and mature enough to really take responsibility for the upbringing of a fledgling. Sure, it's abused by those in power, but there are sound arguments for it. It's open for plenty of abuse, but some amount of population control is necessary to keep the mortals from being aware of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T18:32:44-07:00","id":1396773,"title":"","content":"What Anarchs could do if they seized control is to reform rules against embracing so that the process can be more fair and not used to consolidate the power of the ruler. For example, each officially recognized faction could take turns having the right to embrace. Maybe a population balance could be maintained or maybe new candidates could be voted on. The authority to embrace will still fall into the hands of the more powerful vampires in a region, but it might be more fair and more evenly distribute power than giving sole authority to the Prince. Then again, the Baron or who ever is in charge still has to harshly punish transgressors or the laws will be frequently broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T18:34:34-07:00","id":1396774,"title":"","content":"How Anarchs taking a city over from the Camarilla is:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/full_circle_revolution.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> At the end of the day, they're still vampires.<br /> <br /> That's my VERY cynical take on the Anarchs (who I love).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-15-2020, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T19:12:35-07:00","id":1396781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396774#post1396774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How Anarchs taking a city over from the Camarilla is:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/full_circle_revolution.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> At the end of the day, they're still vampires.<br /> <br /> That's my VERY cynical take on the Anarchs (who I love).</div> </div> </div> </div>Great use of a Chick Track. Considering what Jack Chick thought of D&amp;D, I wonder what he would have thought of Vampire.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think that Anarchs probably are a lot like that, along with real world revolutionaries a lot of the time. The revolution is to change leaders, not really empower the majority of people/vampires. <br /> <br /> If Anarchs institute some kind of democratic system, then who gets to embrace really becomes important, because it\u2019s the power to make new voters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T08:18:00-07:00","id":1396875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396773#post1396773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Anarchs could do if they seized control is to reform rules against embracing so that the process can be more fair and not used to consolidate the power of the ruler. For example, each officially recognized faction could take turns having the right to embrace. Maybe a population balance could be maintained or maybe new candidates could be voted on. The authority to embrace will still fall into the hands of the more powerful vampires in a region, but it might be more fair and more evenly distribute power than giving sole authority to the Prince. Then again, the Baron or who ever is in charge still has to harshly punish transgressors or the laws will be frequently broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mayby saying at the Anarchs everyone after they are not anymore a Fledgeling has one free pass to Embrace anyone. So you can guarentee to have at least one child. If you want more your child need either to be slayn by someone else or you need to convince the others that your second wanted child is worth it or you are worth to Embrace more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T09:21:17-07:00","id":1396889,"title":"","content":"Imagine the unending, projected resentment a sire would feel towards their single legitimate childe after meeting a mortal they like more or would find more useful. That's a bit of angst for the backstory, albeit one better suited for ancillae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T12:01:05-07:00","id":1396911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396677#post1396677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think this is remotely the case for a large number of Embraces. Plenty of people get Embraced on the spur of the moment based on frenzying, overfeeding, Toreador flaw, a subject dying, or whim.<br /> <br /> There's also people who will be Embraced on immediate need.<br /> <br /> &quot;I need a vampire lawyer or a rich guy to bail me out or a soldier for the cause.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I imagine the vast majority of Kindred Embraces are going to be people who can properly disappeared. You can't Embrace Rhianna or Elon Musk. That would be too dangerous to the Masquerade. You can maybe Embrace Rhianna's backup singer or someone who might have become Rhianna should circumstances have not been them. Maybe Elon Musk's right hand man.<br /> <br /> Bob the Plumber or Betty the Florist have as high a chance of being Embraced as, say, Paul the Navy Seal too because it's as likely they'd be Embraced by someone who loves them like their boyfriend or girlfriend who feed on them regularly as Paul for his skillz.<br /> <br /> But that's just my take.<br /> <br /> I think history has shown that the vast majority of human decisions are governed by emotion rather than cold logic and that would certainly apply to the relatively easy act of granting immortality via a bit of blood after feeding.<br /> <br /> YMMV of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of your statement pretty much sums up the paradoxical fluff I am talking about.<br /> <br /> Some one like a Music Star or Inventor/Business person being too high profile to embrace is purely a logical statement, while at the same time claiming that most of human and there for vampiric decisions are emotional in nature and thus a Toredaor actually would embrace Rhianna despite the high profile nature. On the other hand how many musicians or other inspired individuals die young? A high profile person can easily be embraced and thus preserved, they just can't be public anymore.<br /> <br /> Further more what you call &quot;immediate need&quot; is predicated on the mortal in question having a skill or background that is some how enhanced by being a vampire rather than just a ghoul, a dominated mortal, or a well paid human who doesn't know about the supernatural.<br /> <br /> While it is a common clich\u00e9 to embrace some one who reminds you of a lost love, that would be such a rare occurrence as to be Deus Ex Machina rather than a default embracing reason.<br /> <br /> To be fair I view most vampire character tropes as being too emo and limited to survive for any length of time, let alone actually reach elder status. Which means that only those with a certain pragmatism, strength of will, and level of self discipline will survive. Sure you can say an arbitrary 100 mortals are embraced and only about 10-25 of them will be of the sort I am talking about, but over time that group will have a higher chance of surviving, which means that the vampire population ends up skewing more towards that personality type because of attrition.<br /> <br /> The issue is that a lot of STs think that to have a story, you need NPCs to be stupid, make emotional decisions, and make mistakes so that the PCs can uncover their plans, be given a storyhook, have a chance to show their own abilities, etc. This line of thinking is how we get movies where when you think about it, the bad guys defeated themselves, rather than the &quot;heroes&quot; actually defeating them.<br /> <br /> But if the only way to survive past your neonate days is to be competent, careful, and powerful, that means every elder has those traits in spades. So exactly why would such a group of competent and careful vampires ever embrace bob the plumber or betty the flourist again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T12:08:27-07:00","id":1396913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396889#post1396889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine the unending, projected resentment a sire would feel towards their single legitimate childe after meeting a mortal they like more or would find more useful. That's a bit of angst for the backstory, albeit one better suited for ancillae.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Sire can't just ghoul the mortal, thus keeping them young and healthy until the vampire has gotten enough favors to earn another childer embrace? There isn't really a reason for resentment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T13:11:58-07:00","id":1396927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396913#post1396913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the Sire can't just ghoul the mortal, thus keeping them young and healthy until the vampire has gotten enough favors to earn another childer embrace? There isn't really a reason for resentment.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much how the Camarilla manages it as I understand. I didn't make myself clear, but I was talking about a hypothetical &quot;one childe for everyone&quot; system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T13:18:09-07:00","id":1396930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396911#post1396911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of your statement pretty much sums up the paradoxical fluff I am talking about.<br /> <br /> Some one like a Music Star or Inventor/Business person being too high profile to embrace is purely a logical statement, while at the same time claiming that most of human and there for vampiric decisions are emotional in nature and thus a Toredaor actually would embrace Rhianna despite the high profile nature. On the other hand how many musicians or other inspired individuals die young? A high profile person can easily be embraced and thus preserved, they just can't be public anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to never make vampire decisions to be smart ones alone because the simple fact is that they are some of the most emotional and petty creatures in existence. Also, you can't actually tell how a person is going to react to the Embrace. You can Embrace Rhianna and if you go to elaborate lengths to make sure the Prince doesn't want to kill you, to make sure that she's able to continue her music career, and to overcome the Herculean challenges to ease her transition--she may end up losing all interest in music, committing suicide, or simply utterly changed by the experience. One big difference from Requiem and Masquerade is vampires in the latter are not frozen in time -- they indeed can and do become wholly different animals than the person that they were in life. It is impossible to tell who is going to be a great vampire or a terrible one by their mortal efforts anymore than it is who is going to be a functional heroin addict or not (and the blood is a much more potent drug).<br /> <br /> Karl the Gas Station Attendant may be profoundly psychologically more fit to be a vampire and last for 1000+ years than Gordon Keaton who, by all accounts, seemed like a good candidate but turns out to be a serial killer once turned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if the only way to survive past your neonate days is to be competent, careful, and powerful, that means every elder has those traits in spades. So exactly why would such a group of competent and careful vampires ever embrace bob the plumber or betty the flourist again? </div> </div> </div>There's another way to survive past your Neonate days and that's be violent and ruthless. You're describing the only way to survive to be an ELDER and that's a different kettle of fish.<br /> <br /> And the only reason Elders become that way is because the vast majority of them die in petty infighting, suicide, or through other methods before they reach 200.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-16-2020, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T18:42:59-07:00","id":1396982,"title":"","content":"A lot of people are arguing what would be logical for Vampires to do. These people aren't wrong, they make good points.<br /> <br /> It's just that people aren't logical, and even those who seem to be carry an unquenchable ember of Illogic deep inside, waiting to manifest. No one is immune, and history has born this out consistently. Vampires are no different, because they're people.<br /> <br /> If anything, highly successful Kindred are uniquely vulnerable to making senseless decisions, because they've become complacent or arrogant. Everyone <i>thinks</i> that if you unlive long enough to be an Elder, that you're uniquely qualified and rational. Which means they're liable to assume everything they do is reasonable or will work out, and that any difficulties that arise are well within their capacity to handle because they're so competent. They aren't necessarily equipped to objectively gauge their own abilities. Nor are they always aware of the myriad factors that might have saved them in the past (independent of any competence on their part), nor what new factors may be at play that change conditions out of their control.<br /> <br /> As for Kindred rules, they're all well and good (or rather not, because they establish unjust hierarchies, but that's another matter). A law on paper is only as strong as the willingness of people to obey it. And whenever someone breaks a law - assuming they were aware of it to begin with - they tend to have reasons for why they think it's okay for them to do it, or simply aren't thinking about the law when they break it.<br /> <br /> You can create all the laws you like. And you can enforce them with whatever means you choose. None of it actually stops a person from doing it, if they really want to, damn the consequences.<br /> <br /> And as much as authorities like to say they're in control and are capable of stopping law-breakers...well, Real Life shows they very rarely are.<br /> <br /> In VtM, the presence of loads of illicit Embraces, Caitiff, Thin Bloods, and the like isn't an artificial way to add variety to the setting. It's a natural consequence of a sufficiently complex society, full of flawed and finite individuals, that is also built around absolute secrecy as a matter of course. It would be more artificial if it were otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T19:16:42-07:00","id":1396990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1396982#post1396982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people are arguing what would be logical for Vampires to do. These people aren't wrong, they make good points.<br /> <br /> It's just that people aren't logical, and even those who seem to be carry an unquenchable ember of Illogic deep inside, waiting to manifest. No one is immune, and history has born this out consistently. Vampires are no different, because they're people.<br /> <br /> If anything, highly successful Kindred are uniquely vulnerable to making senseless decisions, because they've become complacent or arrogant. Everyone <i>thinks</i> that if you unlive long enough to be an Elder, that you're uniquely qualified and rational. Which means they're liable to assume everything they do is reasonable or will work out, and that any difficulties that arise are well within their capacity to handle because they're so competent. They aren't necessarily equipped to objectively gauge their own abilities. Nor are they always aware of the myriad factors that might have saved them in the past (independent of any competence on their part), nor what new factors may be at play that change conditions out of their control.<br /> <br /> As for Kindred rules, they're all well and good (or rather not, because they establish unjust hierarchies, but that's another matter). A law on paper is only as strong as the willingness of people to obey it. And whenever someone breaks a law - assuming they were aware of it to begin with - they tend to have reasons for why they think it's okay for them to do it, or simply aren't thinking about the law when they break it.<br /> <br /> You can create all the laws you like. And you can enforce them with whatever means you choose. None of it actually stops a person from doing it, if they really want to, damn the consequences.<br /> <br /> And as much as authorities like to say they're in control and are capable of stopping law-breakers...well, Real Life shows they very rarely are.<br /> <br /> In VtM, the presence of loads of illicit Embraces, Caitiff, Thin Bloods, and the like isn't an artificial way to add variety to the setting. It's a natural consequence of a sufficiently complex society, full of flawed and finite individuals, that is also built around absolute secrecy as a matter of course. It would be more artificial if it were otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree 100%<br /> <br /> I admit, I like the fact that this was the case in the original Chicago by Night that had a lot of fascinating reasons for people to do the things they did and Embrace the childer that they did.<br /> <br /> * Balthazar embraced Neon because as much of a bastard as he is, he was horrified at killing a 7 year old boy.<br /> * Critias embraced Damien because he drained a 14 year old boy for the same reason.<br /> * Theodore Dooley Embraced Gordon Keaton because he hated the man and wanted him to suffer horribly as a vampire (and failed to anticipate Gordon was a narcissistic psychopath).<br /> * Lodin did Embrace Ballard, Jackson, and Capone for being extremely capable lieutenants.<br /> * Lodin fucked up royally by Embracing Jacob Schumpeter because he couldn't personally evaluate his daylight connections/lack of skill.<br /> * Nero Embraced Kathy Tyers because she's possibly the greatest guitarist who ever lived but that's not going to be something that impacts most of the rest of her life since she's an otherwise garage band-style person.<br /> * Khalid Embraced two sexually abused children because it related to his misguided quest for Golconda.<br /> * Nicolai Embraced Erichtho for love and Dusable for skill [but also because he needed a strong adult male authority figure to feel comfortable].<br /> * Annabelle embraced Sophia and Brett Stryker because, at the end of the day, Annabelle is a thirsty as suck bisexual woman who loves strippers [and believes it's &quot;art&quot;]. Most Toreador would never think of her choices as justified.<br /> <br /> Because even when they have a REALLY GOOD reason for what they do, it can be a reason other than, &quot;Choose a capable strong-willed genius who will help us rule the world behind the scenes.&quot;<br /> <br /> One thing I liked about THE CHICAGO FOLIOS is one of the NPCs introduced is Alan Sovereign's first known childer--who turns out to be an Armenian plumber. Alan is not the kind of person you would think would Embrace a working class woman but he appreciated someone who actually worked for a living over all the pampered assholes he was surrounded by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-16-2020, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T19:59:52-07:00","id":1396997,"title":"","content":"This thread needs a song...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dMI6B734Ew4\" data-code=\"dMI6B734Ew4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/dMI6B734Ew4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T23:57:43-07:00","id":1397013,"title":"","content":"Re: Tragedy. I tend to focus less on the idea and more on what the purpose of that idea is. Tragedy is one way to create an interesting narrative and character and successfully role play. It's not the *ONLY* way to do it, and it's not necessarily the most interesting way. It will depend on the player and the group/storyteller they're working with. As long as you can build some sort of interesting and enjoyable narrative on it that works for all concerned, whether or not its tragic (and how it might be) is of secondary importance. It's good to remember that the storyteller system can have alot of good ideas that don't always translate well in execution so you may have to look past certain things to see what lies beneath (the 'tragedy' elements might be a 'could have been done better' element. I tended to view the 90s era effort in a similar way, and ignored it when it suited my purposes.) <br /> <br /> Re: Anarchs and Embrace.. would kinda depend on the kind of vampires we're talking about I think. The Duskborn/Thin-blooded are going to be different both mechanically (difficulty in embracing) and institutionally (why they might do it, how they handle it, etc.) than what the more 'older' and 'normal' vampires do. And what they can/can't get away with would also be different (I think thinbloods would both have more trouble creating new vampires which might impose interesting restraints - you aren't going to embrace your loved ones if there is a chance you could kill them in the process. And when you consider many thinbloods may have been created simply as cannon fodder they may not consider the embrace worth offering, either. At the same time they're also likely to have qualities that enable them to thrive/fit in better than other vampires do, and may be more inclined towards a team effort. Sorta like Jenna Cross' group.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T01:38:57-07:00","id":1397019,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I agree with all the reasons you listed why a vampire might Embrace someone.<br /> <br /> You really think Annabelle\u2019s that thirsty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T01:41:41-07:00","id":1397020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1397019#post1397019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I agree with all the reasons you listed why a vampire might Embrace someone.<br /> <br /> You really think Annabelle\u2019s that thirsty?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm exaggerating for comic effect but I think it's a perfectly valid interpretation she embraced both her stripper childer purely because she found them hot. One of the things about the Embrace is that it's often going to be something that people use to create companions rather than business partners.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Toreador are the &quot;lonely creatures of the night&quot; believers but every Clan but the Tremere and Giovanni made vampires out of lovers as well as friends in addition to resources.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T01:54:29-07:00","id":1397022,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> very good point. My female Tremere was Embraced by a male ancilla cause he liked her and thought she was hot, and my Ventrue was Embraced by a member of her family in Ancient Rome for political purposes (much as most if not all of the Giovanni are). So yeah, except for the so-called \u201cmistakes,\u201d I think almost everyone who\u2019s Embraced is someone their Sire thinks is important in some way, whether as a friend, a family member, a love interest, a useful resource or just eye candy (in Annabelle\u2019s case).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T11:00:01-07:00","id":1397332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395408-so-pcs-must-have-suffering-or-tragedy-in-their-backstories?p=1395414#post1395414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are playing a Vampire game something bad has happened to the PCs: they are now dead and need to drink the blood of the living to sustain themselves, there's no way around that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless your characters opinion is similar to a few in Key &amp; Peeles Vampir